    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="1277" n="1127" xml:id="pg1127"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Hill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-04-30"><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 83.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By a decree dated April 16, 1907, published
                    in the Gaceta Oficial of the 18th of the same month, the provisional governor of
                    the Republic of Cuba has accepted the invitation of His Majesty the Emperor of
                    Russia to the Government of Cuba to send delegates to the Second Peace
                    Conference at The Hague.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
